      "final_disposition": "not-applicable",
      "decision": "The full six-file patch changes the modern MDC native-input thumb path, circular hit testing, iOS focus/transition behavior, delayed input-width reset and the modern public constructor/API guard. The owned legacy component has one div thumb, host mouse/touch listeners and host CVA value logic, not projected native input directives or separate visual/range thumbs. Its untouched16.2.14 DOM and eight constructor/focus/pointer/lifetime/value handlers remain exactly preserved. Those modern input-width and circle-hit-test paths are absent across the complete current product source. Replacing them would introduce modern input DOM and alter the historical interaction/constructor contract, outside the owned legacy scope. Do not adopt this modern implementation into the legacy slider. This is not an iOS Safari runtime pass or an inherited peer-fix claim.",
